\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{frap}
\title{Further connections}

\p{The \vocabk{total-orientation character}{frap-000S} can expose a constraint,
but what survives when we change the \vocabk{local frame}{frap-000Q} or the
dimension? \vocabk{Framed orientations}{frap-000A} and [transfer and
dimension](frap-000B) develop the first connections: \vocabk{wreath product}{frap-000Q}
records positions and local transport, while
\vocabk{abelianized characters}{frap-000S} detect constraints when the
allowed generators preserve them
\citet{Section 3.1}{marchetti2025rubik}.
\vocabk{Finite-index transfer}{frap-000W} organizes related calculations through coset
representatives \citet{Sections 3.1--3.3}{mayer2015artin}.
The [dimension calculation](frap-0013) explains how a local
\vocabk{abelianization}{frap-000S} can lose this detecting power without
deciding reachability.}

\p{The following outlooks ask different questions about transport and
functions on a move group. Each needs its own construction; neither is a
prerequisite for continuing to the [layered cubes](frap-0003).}

\transclude{frap-0014}
\transclude{frap-0015}
